## Track 6: Performance & Scalability 🟡

### 6.1 — O(n) Full-Graph Scan on Every Turn
- **File:** [graph.py](file:///e:/AGI/aria/world/graph.py#L388-L461)
- **Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM
- **Finding:** `retrieve_relevant_context()` iterates over *every node* in the graph on every cognitive turn. At 10,000 nodes, this adds measurable latency.
- **Fix:** Build a keyword→node_id inverted index on `load()`. Query the index instead of scanning.

### 6.2 — Duplicate Detection Loads 50 Memories Per Insert
- **File:** [memory_store.py](file:///e:/AGI/aria/memory/memory_store.py#L254-L281)
- **Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM
- **Finding:** Every `add()` call fetches the 50 most recent memories and compares word sets in Python. At high memory counts, this is slow.
- **Fix:** Use a content hash (e.g., normalized sorted words → SHA256) stored as an indexed column. Check the hash before insert.

### 6.3 — Similar Node Detection is O(n) on Graph
- **File:** [graph.py](file:///e:/AGI/aria/world/graph.py#L137-L152)
- **Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM
- **Finding:** `find_similar_node()` iterates all graph nodes for every new node insertion. Same as 6.1 — needs an index.

### 6.4 — Context Prompt Can Grow Unbounded
- **File:** [context_builder.py](file:///e:/AGI/aria/core/context_builder.py#L52-L123)
- **Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM
- **Finding:** The system prompt concatenates: identity (~8KB) + graph context + memories + contradictions + hypotheses + goals + history + stats + tools + principles + skills. With a large graph and many skills, this can exceed the model's context window.
- **Fix:** Add a `MAX_PROMPT_CHARS` budget. Prioritize sections and truncate the lowest-priority ones first.

